{%- comment -%}
  RIZO SKY — the fixed environment behind every page.

  Sections are surfaces laid over it: data-surface="open" lets the sky show
  through, "solid" covers it. That single rule is what makes the moon,
  fog and bats appear between sections instead of on top of the store.

  Where the moon sits is route art direction (assets/rizo.css → "Sky
  positions"). The event layer fills the back stage; with no event live
  the sky is only night tone.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="sky" data-sky aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="sky-tone"></div>
  {% render 'rizo-event-stage', layer: 'back' %}
</div>
